WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.092
This six-stage workflow organizes the module.

00:00:03.092 --> 00:00:06.087
Profile first. Preserve the source.

00:00:06.087 --> 00:00:09.132
Normalize representation where the rule is known.

00:00:09.132 --> 00:00:11.982
Validate values against documented rules.

00:00:11.982 --> 00:00:15.832
Resolve duplicates or questionable rows with explicit logic.

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:21.282
Finally, move stable rules closer to data entry through constraints or monitoring.

00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:26.712
The order matters because prevention should come after you understand the data and the rules.

00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:31.747
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:31.747 --> 00:00:37.932
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:37.932 --> 00:00:40.347
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:40.347 --> 00:00:45.962
In a real setting such as a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields,

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:53.357
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:53.357 --> 00:00:55.552
before discussing syntax.

00:00:55.552 --> 00:01:01.600
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
